{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","cve_id":"CVE-2026-110725","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","summary":"fast-uri vulnerable to scheme injection via an unescaped first-segment colon in suffix references","description":"### Impact\n\n`fast-uri`'s `serialize()`, `normalize()`, and `resolve()`, when called with the non-default option `reference: 'suffix'` on a reference that has no authority, emit a relative reference whose first path segment contains a bare colon without escaping it. RFC 3986 section 3.3 requires the first segment of a `path-noscheme` reference not to contain a colon, precisely because a bare colon makes the string reparse as an absolute URI with a scheme. `fast-uri`'s default serialization escapes that colon, but the suffix path does not.\n\nFor example, `normalize('javascript:alert(1)', { reference: 'suffix' })` returns `javascript:alert(1)`, which reparses as a live `javascript:` scheme; `data:` and `vbscript:` behave the same.\n\nApplications that serialize or normalize a relative reference with `reference: 'suffix'` and then treat the result as a URI can turn inert input into a live `javascript:`, `data:`, or `vbscript:` URL (a cross-site scripting vector), and `equal()` can conflate a scheme-bearing reference with a relative one. Exposure is limited to applications that use the non-default `reference: 'suffix'` option.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to `fast-uri` `2.4.8`, `3.1.9`, or `4.2.3`.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nDo not use the `reference: 'suffix'` option on untrusted input. If suffix output is required, percent-encode a colon in the first path segment of the result before treating it as a URI.","type":"reviewed","severity":"low","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fast-uri/security-advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","source_code_location":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-110725","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110725","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/39e6493c1356f30a0084171627eb266786e1620e","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/a9b8d67353630aab053cd727cf629023dd018d2b","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.8","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.9","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.2.3","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp"],"published_at":"2026-10-23T21:36:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T21:36:41Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-10-23T21:36:40Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-10-20T07:17:08Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 2.4.8","first_patched_version":"2.4.8","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.0.0, < 3.1.9","first_patched_version":"3.1.9","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 4.0.0, < 4.2.3","first_patched_version":"4.2.3","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","score":3.7},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-41","name":"Improper Resolution of Path Equivalence"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-116","name":"Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"UlisesGascon","id":5110813,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTA4MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5110813?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/UlisesGascon","html_url":"https://github.com/UlisesGascon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UlisesGascon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/UlisesGascon/following{